  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">e-transformation of policing processes related to contravention UNDP 2022-2027 - Supporting e-transformation of policing processes related to contravention cases</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">e-transformation of policing processes related to contravention UNDP 2022-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Bidraget kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras av UNDP Moldavien och kommer att ha en teknisk karakt&#xe4;r: skapandet av en ny mjukvara f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att brotten i Moldavien registreras p&#xe5; digitala s&#xe4;tt, vilket minskar m&#xe4;nsklig faktor och korruption; och att se till att utredningen av brott g&#xf6;rs i r&#xe4;tt tid och med fullt ansvar av polisen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The contribution will be implemented by UNDP Moldova and will have a technical character: the creation of a new soft to ensure the offences in Moldova are registered using digital ways therefore diminishing human factor and corruption; and ensuring the investigation of offences is done in due time and with full accountability by the police.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The new e-contravention case management system, developed through this intervention (conceptualisation, development, piloting, stabilization and roll-out and maintenance), will support the optimization of policing activities in contravention procedure, will improve discipline and institutional control over the contravention cases, will enhance the quality of data produced during the documentation of contraventions, will facilitate the exchange of data between MoI and other justice chain institutions with responsibilities in contravention cases (e.g. prosecution, courts). Furthermore, the new e-contravention case management system will harmonize and enhance collaboration among the 44 state institutions/agents with a mandate to detect and investigate contraventions.Considering the applicable legal provisions and procedures, the e-contravention case management system will ensure the interoperability with case management systems of prosecution and judiciary through the M-Connect e-service. Taken together, these results can increase public confidence in and support for law enforcement and justice processes, enhancing system performance and, ultimately, the integrity of the law.</narrative>
  </description>
